<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tarhunt</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Tarhun</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tarhunt, also called Tarhun, was the storm god of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hittite-empire">Hittites</a> and other Anatolian peoples and one of the chief deities of the Hittite pantheon. The Hittite king ruled as the earthly representative of the storm god rather than as a god himself. This created a more negotiated relationship between royal and priestly authority than existed under Egyptian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/divine-kingship">divine kingship</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tarhunt.jpg" alt="Tarhunt" width="320" height="428" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Verity Cridland · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hetite_God_in_Aleppo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
